  "id": "COMPOUND:4343 - PROTEIN:6151",
  "verbalization": "Cycloleucine appears to interact with Ataxin-2 through a series of molecular pathways, with the central node being the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase. This enzyme is targeted by multiple compounds, including 2-Methylheptyl propanoate and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, all of which ultimately lead to the activation of Ataxin-2. The evidence suggests that Cycloleucine may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the modulation of this enzyme, potentially influencing the activity of Ataxin-2 in a cellular context. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Cycloleucine in modulating the function of Ataxin-2 via a complex network of enzymatic interactions, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
